============================================================================
THE CERTIFICATE COCHAIN (QR/Paley sign) + soundness on complex 1
============================================================================
  certificate = coboundary of the Paley/QR vertex-sign: it is a cocycle (d1=0 on all squares)? True (violations=0); it is a COBOUNDARY by construction => LOCALLY TESTABLE (vertex-differences).
  soundness sample (200 pseudo-random 1-cochains): mean rejection |d1 g|/|F| = 0.467, min = 0.429, max = 0.496
  => nonzero rejection on generic words = the square test DETECTS non-cocycles; combined with b1=14
     (complex 1) the coboundary structure determines local testability of the certificate.

============================================================================
READ: b1 tells whether the apex complex KILLS the anti-LTC obstruction (b1=0) or retains nontrivial
certificate classes (b1>0). The Paley/QR certificate is realized as a COBOUNDARY (locally testable)
when it lifts to im(d0). This is the explicit co-cycle encoding + the soundness (coboundary) test.
============================================================================
